        ],
        "text": "A Gandharva marriage—or did you dream it up?",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s041-u044",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s041-d032",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 56,
            "printedPage": 48
          }
        ],
        "text": "A registered marriage.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s041-u045",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பரந்தாமன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s041-d033",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 56,
            "printedPage": 48
          }
        ],
        "text": "A registered marriage. I am here—there is still a man in this house. A registered marriage without my knowing....",
        "notes": [
          "The source syntax and punctuation are irregular here; the English retains the broken, indignant delivery rather than smoothing it into a new sentence."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s041-u050",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s041-d037",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 56,
            "printedPage": 48
          }
        ],
        "text": "You live in this house? At least the word 'house' has come from your mouth—that alone makes me happy!...",
        "notes": [
          "Recovered explicitly labelled source utterance; new translation unit added without renumbering historical translation-unit IDs."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s041-u051",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பரந்தாமன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s041-d038",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 56,
            "printedPage": 48
          }
        ],
        "text": "Akka! I understand you now. I understand that all the affection you showed, calling me 'little brother, little brother,' was mere pretence. Otherwise, after telling me as though affection overflowed, 'Kumudha lives for you; she is your wife,' would you now say that you have made her the wife of some orphaned fellow!",
        "notes": [
          "Recovered explicitly labelled source utterance; new translation unit added without renumbering historical translation-unit IDs."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s041-u046",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s041-d034",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 56,
            "printedPage": 48
          },
          {
            "pdfPage": 57,
            "printedPage": 49
          }
        ],
        "text": "Why do you need a wife? Whenever you wish, wives are available to you! For those beauties who ask for wealth without asking for love, there are innocent workers to pawn to the mill owner so that you can lavish money on them...",
        "notes": [
          "This labelled utterance crosses PDF 56→57 and remains one translation unit.",
          "Corrected-source reconciliation replaces the historical mistranscription of `அன்பைக் கேட்- / காமல் ஐஸ்வரியத்தைக் கேட்கும்` while preserving the genuine physical page split."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s041-u047",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பரந்தாமன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s041-d035",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 57,
            "printedPage": 49
          }
        ],
        "text": "Enough, stop!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s041-u048",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s041-d036",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 57,
            "printedPage": 49
          }
        ],
        "text": "Intelligent! Pure! I expected praises like these to come to you. I never imagined words of blame like 'debauchee' and 'wrongdoer' would come instead.",
        "notes": []
      },
